● The file is done. Here's a summary of what was added to cluster_driver.jl:

  ClusterPlotConfig — Base.@kwdef struct controlling everything:
  - pixel_size_nm, colormap, scalebar — passed straight to
  RenderConfig/GaussianRender
  - show_centroids, centroid_size, centroid_color — × markers at each cluster
  centroid
  - boundaries — optional ClusterBoundaryInfo; when set, draws alpha-shape
  outlines
  - boundary_linewidth — line weight for those outlines
  - filename, figure_size — output control

  plot_clusters(smld, smld_out, cfg) — five steps:
  1. Calls render(smld, RenderConfig(...)) with GaussianRender to produce the
  density background
  2. Re-derives the same physical μm bounds that SMLMRender used internally
  (data extrema + 5 % margin), so the CairoMakie axis aligns exactly with the
  image pixels
  3. Builds a Figure/Axis with yreversed=true (SMLM y increases downward) and
  calls image! with a transposed image (permutedims(bg_img, (2,1)) converts
  [row,col]=[y,x] to [col,row]=[x,y] as Makie expects)
  4. Scatters × markers at each cluster centroid
  5. If cfg.boundaries !== nothing, draws each boundary polygon with cycled
  colours from a qualitative palette

  The driver body was updated to use distinct config variable names (cfg_dbscan,
   cfg_bnd, cfg_hop) and calls plot_clusters with binfo saving a PNG named after
   the data file.

