Summary

  Added every statistic from dev/boundary/STATISTICS to
  src/backends/statistics.jl that wasn't already covered by ClusterInfo
  (n_clusters/n_points/n_clustered/n_isolated were skipped as pre-existing):

  - ClusterBoundaryStatisticsInfo grew from 5 fields to 27: boundary
  indices/area/perimeter at three tightnesses (general, convex-hull, tightest
  alpha-shape), shape descriptors (equiv_radii, compactness, circularity,
  convexity, solidity), point-count stats (center, n_pts_per_cluster,
  n_pts_per_area, sigma_actual, cluster_width, nn_within_clust), and
  inter-cluster spacing (min_c2c_dists/min_e2e_dists and their scalar minima).
  - boundary_statistics gained a per_dataset::Bool=true keyword so it can
  regroup smld_out emitters per cluster the same way boundary_clusters did;
  area/perimeter computation is untouched (still derived purely from binfo's
  stored polygon), and every new field degrades to NaN/empty rather than
  throwing when a cluster has no matching raw points.
  - Updated dev/boundary/cluster_driver.jl's call site and
  test/test_boundary.jl's positional-constructor tests and assertions
  accordingly.

  Both test tiers pass (305/305 fast, 1218/1218 full). One note worth flagging:
  convexity (perimeterConvex / perimeterTight) isn't bounded above by 1 the way
  the STATISTICS doc's description implies — the shrink=1 "tightest" alpha shape
  from the existing boundary_cluster keeps only the largest boundary loop,
  which can trace a small sub-triangle of the cluster rather than an enclosing
  curve, occasionally making it shorter than the convex hull's perimeter. That's
  inherent to the pre-existing boundary_cluster algorithm, not something
  introduced here — documented in the code and test comments rather than
  "fixed."

